      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "***PRIME CITY CENTRE INVESTMENT OPPORTUNITY / HEART OF TEMPLE BAR / EXCELLENT RENTAL LOCATION / DUAL ACCESS FROM ASTON QUAY & BEDFORD LANE / CLOSE TO ALL AMENITIES & TRANSPORT LINKS***\r\n\r\nKelly Bradshaw is delighted to present Apartment 2, 10 Aston Abbey, Aston Quay, an attractive and well-appointed one-bedroom apartment extending to approximately 44 sq.m., superbly positioned in the heart of Dublin 2's vibrant Temple Bar district.\r\n\r\nPresented in excellent condition throughout, the apartment offers bright, well-designed accommodation with high ceilings, excellent natural light and a layout carefully designed to maximise both comfort and functionality. The property benefits from an upgraded heating system, a modern fitted kitchen and bathroom, and a generous double bedroom, making it an ideal choice for owner-occupiers, investors or those seeking a centrally located Dublin residence.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation provides a welcoming living space complemented by a modern kitchen area, comfortable double bedroom and contemporary bathroom facilities. The overall presentation and efficient layout create a stylish and practical home in one of Dublin's most sought-after city-centre locations.\r\n\r\nSituated on Aston Quay in the centre of Temple Bar, Apartment 2 enjoys immediate access to an exceptional range of restaurants, cafés, entertainment venues, cultural attractions and city-centre amenities. The Irish Film Institute, Smock Alley Theatre, Temple Bar Gallery & Studios, Meeting House Square and The Button Factory are all within easy walking distance.\r\n\r\nThe apartment is also ideally located close to Dublin's principal business, financial, educational and retail districts, making it particularly appealing to  and those seeking the convenience of city-centre living.The property benefits from outstanding public transport connections, with numerous Dublin Bus services nearby, the LUAS Red Line within easy reach, and both Tara Street and Pearse Street railway stations within walking distance. Dublin Airport is also easily accessible via public transport links.\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended and available through Kelly Bradshaw."
      },
